WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.134
-After signaling

00:00:02.134 --> 00:00:03.937
that they were willing
to do anything possible

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.606
to sabotage
President Joe Biden's agenda,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.109
Senate Republicans
are now supposedly upset

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.576
that Joe Biden
won't work with them.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.645
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:16.516
♪♪

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:19.018
Even as new reported coronavirus
infections are dropping,

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:20.186
things are still very bad

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.588
and will likely stay that way
for a while.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.290
With new, more transmissible
variants identified,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.725
at this point, it's a race

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.193
between the variants
and the vaccines

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:28.728
and, seeing as how
the last administration

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.696
left the vaccine rollout
in chaos,

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:32.132
with some getting tossed
in the garbage

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.233
and others missing altogether,
there's a lot of work to do.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:37.570
I mean, the Trump administration
passed on the opportunity

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.205
to buy more vaccine
when they had it.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.508
Such a simple solution,
and they just missed it.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.743
If Trump ever tried
an escape room,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.812
they'd just find a skeleton
slumped over the first clue.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:50.349
"Jesus! He's only been
in there for an hour."

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:51.584 line:0%
Seriously, what was their plan,

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.586 line:0%
send everyone a tin of Altoids

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.920 line:0%
filled with hydroxychloroquine,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.457
wait for Redditors to drive up
Pfizer's stock price?

00:00:58.457 --> 00:00:59.859
"Mr. President,
why did you short

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:02.128
a million dollars' worth
of Pfizer stock?"

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.763
[ As Trump ]
I'm waiting for those GameStop
nerds to drive up the price.

00:01:04.763 --> 00:01:06.966
"But you're supposed to buy it,
not short it."

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.334
Oh, no!

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.137
[ Laughter ]
Oh, no!

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.505
Oh, quick.
Call my broker.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:13.639
"Who's your broker?"

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.275
[ As Trump ]
Okay, I'm going to tell you,

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.342
but no judgment.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.610
It's Rudy.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:21.147
I think he might be bad
at this, too.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.284 line:0%
I told him to short GameStop
and he showed up like this.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.553
They don't sell those shorts.

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.055
He went out and had them made.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.323
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.259
Also, how does a lifesaving
vaccine just go missing?

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.161
If Trump were part
of an elite heist squad

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.396
that stole the Hope Diamond,

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:37.897
he'd immediately stuff it
in his pocket,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.766
forget about it, and then
throw it in the toll basket

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.167
with the rest of his change.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.268
[ As Trump ]
Alright, guys,
good news, bad news.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.603
Bad news --
I lost the diamond.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.005
Good news is I've decided
to get E-ZPass,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:49.175
which I think is going to be
helpful for future heists.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.111
Also bad news -- I think I threw
my driver's license

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.047
in with the diamond, so,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.749
stay away from the
safe house, guys.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:58.951
States have begging the federal
government for more vaccine,

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.853
which the Trump administration
just didn't provide,

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:03.223
but, now, just a week
into the Biden administration,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.391
significant progress
has already been made.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.827 line:8%
-Big announcement from the
Biden administration today.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.061 line:14%
They say they have purchased

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:11.664 line:8%
200 million
additional vaccine doses,

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.266 line:8%
which will be delivered
over the summer,

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.901 line:8%
providing the U.S.
with enough doses

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:18.271 line:8%
to vaccinate a total
of 300 million Americans.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.473
-Wait, so it was possible
to buy more vaccine

00:02:21.473 --> 00:02:23.776
this whole time,
and Trump just didn't do it?

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:27.246
What else was he doing,
having his gloves tightened?

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.582
Was he working on his
Jerry Lewis impression?

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.819
-We're going to walk down to the
[ raises voice ] Capitol!

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:36.822
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.525
-Real nice find, Baze.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.360
I thought the one thing
Trump was good at

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.363
was buying things with money
that wasn't technically his.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:45.698
I guess that explains

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.800
that famous passage
in "The Art of the Deal"...

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:55.874
Biden announced the plan
to buy more vaccine on Tuesday

00:02:55.874 --> 00:02:57.944
and gave the American people
a rough timeline

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.346
of when they could expect
the doses to arrive.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.714
-So today I'm directing

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:05.050
COVID-19 Response Coordinator
Jeff Zients, here,

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.520
to work with the Department
of Health and Human Services

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.521
and increase our total supply

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:12.225
of vaccine
for the American people.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:15.761
That's 100 million
more doses of Pfizer

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.730
and 100 million more doses
of Moderna --

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.499
200 million more doses

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.968
than the federal government
had previously secured.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.405
We expect these additional
200 million doses

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.707
to be delivered this summer.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.375
-So the president
did a competent thing

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.377
to address the crisis,
announced it in clear

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.212
and simple terms
Americans could understand,

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:34.647
and he offered
a rough timetable,

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.516
so he could be held accountable,

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.283
and he did it
without barking at reporters

00:03:38.283 --> 00:03:41.554
next to a worrying helicopter
about how some random celebrity

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.956
was nice to him in 1987
or whatever.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.859
[ As Trump ]
Jack Nicklaus,
"The Golden Bear."

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.028
Never met a chip shot
he couldn't make.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.230
Real son of a bitch.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.598
Nasty guy.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.134
Nice to me, though.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.670
Heard they call him "The Bear"
because he [bleep] in the woods.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.105
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.606
A lot of people are saying it.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.475
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.877
Look, Joe Biden is inevitably
going to make mistakes,

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.278
as all presidents do,

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.347
and there will be times
when we'll have to push him

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:10.283
on progressive priorities
and hold him accountable,

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.585
but with all that said,
it's just a relief

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.454
to have competent administration
of government again.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:15.788
People just want things to work.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.824
Instead, Republicans
intentionally wreck things,

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:18.957
so they can turn around and say,

00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:20.426
"Look, government is bad.
We should cut it."

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.061
Ted Cruz basically says,
every day --

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.362
[ As Cruz ]
Do you really want a man like me

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.597
making decisions for you?

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:27.400
A man who, every morning,
puts glue on his face,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.268
then walks to the nearest barber

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:31.237
and rubs his cheeks
in the clippings."

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:34.807
And, now, Republicans are eager
to let Trump off the hook

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:37.176
for inciting a violent mob
to overrun the Capitol

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.946
because he's popular
with GOP voters.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.682
That's basically the point
Lindsey Graham tried to make

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.583
in an interview last night
on Fox News.

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.885 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.154 line:8%
-Here, now,
Senator Lindsey Graham.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.188
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.989
Was that a a pick, Lindsey,

00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:54.026
or were you doing a last-minute
coronavirus test?

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.728
[ As Graham ]
Dang, I forgot my swab.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.964
Good thing I was born
with ten of them.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:59.865
Or maybe that was just
the last place left

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.467
he hadn't checked
for his conscience.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.869
I mean, what were you going
to do with it, anyway, keep it?

00:05:03.869 --> 00:05:06.706
[ Graham ]
When I find a good one,
I keep it as a pet.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.174
This one's Bessie over here,

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:10.209
this one's Clyde,
and this one's

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.845
Braxton Beauregard
Bridgerton III.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.347
He's my best friend.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.714
Mama, when Daddy gets back,

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:17.350
I'm going to show him
my booger collection.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.785
What?!

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:21.020
What do you mean,
he's not coming back?

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.755
Why?

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.691
Because of the
booger collection.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:28.761
Well, I miss you, Daddy,
but I made my choice!

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.029
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:33.199
I forgot why I was even going
to play that clip.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:35.868
Oh, right.
The day before that, on Tuesday,

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.237
Lindsey Graham
had a bone to pick

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.573
if Democrats call witnesses
in the impeachment trial

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.441
and then threaten
to prolong the proceedings.

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.443 line:8%
-If there's an effort
by the Democrats

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:47.814 line:8%
to call a single witness
in the United States Senate

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:49.915 line:7%
that had no record in the House,

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.617 line:8%
there will be delay
of this trial.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.653 line:0%
There will be a Pandora's box
being opened.

00:05:54.653 --> 00:05:55.988 line:0%
We will want witnesses

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.657 line:0%
and this thing will go on
for weeks, if not months.

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:01.193
-Oh, no, don't do that.
Witnesses? In a trial?

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:02.495
What's next, evidence?

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.630
Lindsey Graham is so bad
at threatening things,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.265
I wouldn't be surprised
if he backed his way

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.900
into calling Trump to the stand.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.169
[ As Graham ]
If Democrats insist
on calling witnesses,

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.738
we'll have no choice
but to call our own witnesses,

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:13.972
like Donald Trump himself.

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:15.475
How would they like that?

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:17.543
They'd love it?
Why?

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:20.179
Because he will most certainly
incriminate himself?

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:24.016
[ Laughing ]
Oh, Braxton Beauregard
Bridgerton III,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.552
I have done it again!

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.054
Back in your menagerie!

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:30.256
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.524 --> 00:06:34.760
In fact, a thorough trial
that brings out all the evidence

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:36.128
would be a good thing!

00:06:36.128 --> 00:06:38.263
It was a violent insurrection
to overthrow democracy,

00:06:38.263 --> 00:06:40.666
the first time the Capitol's
been breached in 200 years.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:43.569
Nearly 140 police officers
were injured during the riot.

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.872 line:0%
And you guys, supposedly
the pro-police party

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:47.873 line:0%
of law and order, want to just
move on and forget about it.

00:06:47.873 --> 00:06:50.376 line:0%
Every time anyone tries
to investigate Trump,

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:52.611
you react like parents trying
to wrap presents

00:06:52.611 --> 00:06:54.279
in the basement
on Christmas morning.

00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:55.915
Don't come down here!

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.184
Mommy and Daddy are
[ Mumbling ]

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.985
having sex!
"Jesus, Steve.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:01.353
That just makes it worse."

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:03.021
I didn't know what to say.
I panicked.

00:07:03.021 --> 00:07:04.389
But, should we?

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:06.125
"No!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.759
Impeachment aside,
Republicans have pledged

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:08.961
to do everything possible

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:10.896
to stonewall and sabotage
Biden's agenda,

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:12.999
despite the fact
that 50 Senate Republicans

00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:15.233
represent 41 million
fewer Americans

00:07:15.233 --> 00:07:17.302
than the 50 Senate Democrats,
not to mention,

00:07:17.302 --> 00:07:20.206
they lost the House
by a record margin in 2018

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.707
and their presidential
candidate lost

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.976
by over seven million votes
in 2020.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:27.012
They just lost two seats
at the same time in Georgia,

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:28.280
a longtime red state.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.749
And, yet, instead of reflecting

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:32.451
on how thoroughly they've been
rejected by voters, and why,

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.854
Republicans are actually
pretending to be upset

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:36.722
the Democrats
won't work with them.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.324
"There's frustration
on the Republican side

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.926
that Biden, Chuck Schumer,
and Democrats appear headed

00:07:40.926 --> 00:07:43.328
toward taking a one-party
approach to Covid relief."

00:07:43.328 --> 00:07:46.165
Oh, I'm so sorry
you're frustrated.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:48.300
I mean, my goodness,
we wouldn't want to upset

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.936
noted advocate of bipartisanship
Mitch McConnell,

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:53.338
who I'm sure is sitting
by a rain-soaked window,

00:07:53.338 --> 00:07:55.207
silently staring
out into the distance,

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:57.776
wondering why no one across the
aisle will work with him,

00:07:57.776 --> 00:08:00.012
only to remember that
he's a coldblooded assassin

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:02.148
who destroys all opposition
in his path,

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:04.516
and only then will he smile.

00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:05.784
Seriously,
when you were in power,

00:08:05.784 --> 00:08:07.319
you steamrolled Democrats
every chance you got --

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:09.421
you nuked the filibuster
for Supreme Court nominees,

00:08:09.421 --> 00:08:11.690
you tried to ram through
a last-minute Obamacare repeal

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.158
without so much as a hearing,

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:15.094
and you literally
scribbled changes

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:17.229
into the margins of a massive
corporate tax cut

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:18.997
in the middle of the night,
like a drunk

00:08:18.997 --> 00:08:20.866
writing his number
down on a bar napkin.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:22.468
"Why don't you
call me sometime?"

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:24.603
Sir, you're talking
to the jukebox.

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:26.972
2020 was the worst year
for economic growth

00:08:26.972 --> 00:08:28.774 line:0%
since World War II.
Millions are unemployed,

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.876 line:0%
losing their health insurance,
and falling into poverty,

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:34.013 line:0%
as child hunger rises
to unprecedented levels.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:36.515 line:0%
It's the worst national
catastrophe in a century

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:37.917 line:0%
and it requires
immediate action.

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:41.120 line:0%
We don't have time to indulge
feigned victimhood

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.355 line:0%
and wounded egos
of Republican senators.

00:08:43.355 --> 00:08:44.956
Thankfully,
Democrats seem to understand

00:08:44.956 --> 00:08:46.959
the urgency of the moment
and are moving quickly.

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:48.794
Today, Senate Majority Leader
Chuck Schumer

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:50.462
promised bold action and said

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:53.465
slimming down the COVID relief
package would be irresponsible.

00:08:53.465 --> 00:08:56.702
And incoming
Senate Budget Committee
Chairman Bernie Sanders

00:08:56.702 --> 00:09:00.139
had said he has no qualms
using budget reconciliation,

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:02.541
a method that requires
only 51 votes,

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:04.176
to pass a massive relief bill.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:06.878 line:15%
-Reconciliation,
which is a Senate rule,

00:09:06.878 --> 00:09:09.448 line:15%
was used by the Republicans
under Trump

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.317 line:14%
to pass massive tax breaks

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:13.451 line:15%
for the rich
and large corporations.

00:09:13.451 --> 00:09:15.488 line:14%
It was used as an attempt

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:18.423 line:15%
to repeal
the Affordable Care Act.

00:09:18.423 --> 00:09:20.292 line:14%
And what we are saying is,

00:09:20.292 --> 00:09:21.793 line:15%
"You used it for that.
That's fine.

00:09:21.793 --> 00:09:23.262 line:15%
"You did it.
We're going to do it,

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:25.965 line:15%
but we're going to do it
to protect ordinary people,

00:09:25.965 --> 00:09:27.533 line:15%
not just the rich
and the powerful."

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:29.235 line:14%
Did I criticize Republicans?

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:32.070 line:15%
Yeah, for using reconciliation
to give tax breaks

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.073 line:15%
to billionaires,
to create a situation

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:35.841 line:15%
where large,
profitable corporations

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:37.943 line:15%
now pay zero
in federal income taxes.

00:09:37.943 --> 00:09:39.644 line:15%
Yes, I did criticize them
for that.

00:09:39.644 --> 00:09:41.280 line:15%
And, if they want
to criticize me

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.116 line:15%
for helping to feed children
who are hungry,

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:45.584 line:15%
or senior citizens
in this country

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.986 line:15%
who are isolated and alone
and don't have enough food,

00:09:47.986 --> 00:09:49.254 line:14%
they can criticize me.

00:09:49.254 --> 00:09:51.022
-Yeah, I have a feeling
GOP criticism

00:09:51.022 --> 00:09:53.092
doesn't make much of a dent
in Bernie Sanders.

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:54.126
Bernie, you're going to wear

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:56.128
those mittens
to the inauguration?

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.163
[ As Sanders ]
You're damn right.
These mittens are warm.

00:09:58.163 --> 00:09:59.932
And, when you freeze to death,

00:09:59.932 --> 00:10:02.000
I'm going to wear these mittens
to your funeral.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.270
I'm going to comfort your widow
with these mittens.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.706
They're there, I'll say.
Now move!

00:10:06.706 --> 00:10:09.641
Bernie knows how to harness
that Grandpa energy for good.

00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:11.376
[ As Sanders ]
You had the remote all morning

00:10:11.376 --> 00:10:12.945
and you used it
to watch cartoons.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:15.114
That's fine,
but, now, it's my turn.

00:10:15.114 --> 00:10:17.383
And I'm going to use it to watch
my cooking program on PBS,

00:10:17.383 --> 00:10:19.018
called...

00:10:19.018 --> 00:10:20.552
[ Laughter ]

00:10:20.552 --> 00:10:23.221
This should be the message --
the days of complicated,

00:10:23.221 --> 00:10:25.124
Rube Goldberg legislation,

00:10:25.124 --> 00:10:28.327
where you provide tax incentives
for job retraining,

00:10:28.327 --> 00:10:30.396
for workforce reentry subsidies,

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:33.565
or whatever the hell Democrats
used to talk about, are over.

00:10:33.565 --> 00:10:35.567
Keep it simple
and make it sound good.

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:36.802
Do it like Republicans do it.

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:38.537
They'll write a bill
that makes food illegal

00:10:38.537 --> 00:10:40.672
and call it
the Feed America bill.

00:10:40.672 --> 00:10:42.941
Republicans use their time
in power

00:10:42.941 --> 00:10:44.476
to dole out tax cuts
for the rich.

00:10:44.476 --> 00:10:46.845
Democrats should use it
to feed children and the elderly

00:10:46.845 --> 00:10:48.414
and then, they can pay for it

00:10:48.414 --> 00:10:50.382
by taxing corporations,
billionaires,

00:10:50.382 --> 00:10:52.784
and all the gold Lindsey Graham
digs up in his -- you know.

00:10:52.784 --> 00:10:55.687
Massive, immediate relief
and large structural change

00:10:55.687 --> 00:10:57.188
are required
to improve people's lives

00:10:57.188 --> 00:10:59.191
and fix
our deeply broken system.

00:10:59.191 --> 00:11:01.427
We don't have time to entertain
the bad faith of Republicans,

00:11:01.427 --> 00:11:04.229
who obviously have no interest
in doing anything about it.

00:11:04.229 --> 00:11:06.465
Democrats need to move fast
and ignore objections

00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:08.566
from Republicans
intent on stonewalling.

00:11:08.566 --> 00:11:10.936
Otherwise, negotiations
over the relief bill will...

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:13.272
-Go on for weeks, if not months.

00:11:13.272 --> 00:11:14.973
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:11:14.973 --> 00:11:18.844
♪♪

00:11:18.844 --> 00:11:20.312
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:11:20.312 --> 00:11:21.613
over two million meals a year

00:11:21.613 --> 00:11:24.116
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:25.717
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:11:25.717 --> 00:11:27.252
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:11:27.252 --> 00:11:29.855
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:31.523
Stay safe.
Wash your hands.

00:11:31.523 --> 00:11:33.259
Wear a mask.
We love you.

